  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="8b1a-6808-ad04-b034" name="Numidian (Hannibal) - List Notes" publicationId="fc9f-8438-629b-e92d" hidden="false">
      <description>NUMIDIAN ARMY LIST (Hannibal &amp; the Punic Wars, pp.74-75)
Characters up to 25%; at least one must be the overall leader; besides a General the army may have an Army Standard Bearer and additional leaders. If no Army General is selected the commander must be a Tribal Leader.
Terrain: the Numidian player may place his generated terrain on his opponent's side of the table; on a roll of 9 (Walls/Hedges) he may place any other terrain instead.
Field Fortifications: after terrain is determined the Numidian player may place 4D6" of linear obstacles or field fortifications on his side of the table at no cost.
Ambush: before deployment the Numidian player may hide one unit anywhere out of sight of the enemy deployment zone and deploy it at the start of his first turn.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS:
[Numidian]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Cavalry: at least 25%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  Standard Numidian composition.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
